---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
---

<Base title="About" description={`About ${site.name}: security engineer by day, photographer and filmmaker the rest of the time, based in New York.`}>
  <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
  <h1>Hi, I'm Johnny.</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      I'm a photographer and developer in New York. Most of what's on this site is work I
      made for communities I belong to, and places I went with a camera.
    </p>

    <p>
      By day I work in security. I build automation in Tines, own our privileged access
      management platform, and review infrastructure proposals from engineering. It's work
      about trust: who gets access to what, and how you know. It also explains the shape of
      the projects here. I care most about systems that keep working after the person who
      built them walks away, so you'll see tokens instead of bespoke CSS, settings the
      client can edit instead of hard-coded copy, and documentation that says why.
    </p>

    <p>
      Lately most of that building has been for
      <a href={url('/projects/gotham-brand-system')}>Gotham Knights RFC</a>, New York's LGBT
      rugby club: the brand system, the website, the storefront, and the drag show's
      look. One club, a lot of surfaces.
    </p>

    <p>
      The photography and video are the part I'd make even if nobody asked. I shoot the
      people and places around me, and I want to make more work about queer athletes and
      the people who hold their communities together. If that's something you're working
      on, I'd like to hear about it.
    </p>

    <h2>Get in touch</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>, or find me on
      {site.links.map((l, i) => (
        <>
          <a href={l.href} target="_blank" rel="me noopener">{l.label}</a>{i < site.links.length - 1 ? ', ' : '.'}
        </>
      ))}
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
